From f2104752fa9da550b3c659d391f7b88167a22131 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:38:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] power: supply: apple_j71t_charger: accept the camera
 adapter as a source

The CBTL1610 supplier now reports the identified Lightning camera adapter
as POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_ACA, also while the iPad is the USB host. Treat
it as an eligible source, like a verified host grant or an Apple brick,
so the policy ramps to the supplier's budget (2100 mA after the power
handshake). The DT ceiling (2400 mA) and the calibrated budget table
already include 2100 mA.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <maintainer@example.invalid>
Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
---
 drivers/power/supply/apple_j71t_charger.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_j71t_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_j71t_charger.c
index ce93beb939..923ad579b4 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_j71t_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/apple_j71t_charger.c
@@ -200,8 +200,10 @@ static int j71t_source_eligible(struct j71t_charger *charger)
 						      POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_USB_TYPE, &value);
 	if (ret)
 		return -EAGAIN;
+	/* ACA: the identified camera adapter, a source while the iPad is the host. */
 	return value.intval == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_SDP ||
-	       value.intval == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_APPLE_BRICK_ID;
+	       value.intval == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_APPLE_BRICK_ID ||
+	       value.intval == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_ACA;
 }
 
 /* Link PM/reset is not source removal; only ONLINE=0 revokes the owner. */
